   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project Outcome</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">An efficient, safe, reliable, road network developed in western Afghanistan.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator 3</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">By 2018:  A decrease in vehicle operating cost or freight and passenger transport fares by 30% 
Progress/Status: The outcome will be assessed upon completion of road construction, the work suspension and subsequent termination of the previous contractor hindered the timely achievement of the project outcome. However, the civil work contracts for section 1 and 2 were signed on 16 September 2017 and Notice to proceed (NTP) were issued on 22 Jan 2018. Section 1 (34km) of the Ring Road progress is at 25.22% against the planned progress of 32.5%. Progress of 48km Section 2 is 16.40% against the planned progress of 39.91%. Slow progress of both sections is due to insufficient machinery and staff at the project site. Work is stopped due to cold weather. Inputs from this grant is completed. 
Data Source: MPW and MOTCA traffic counts, surveys and reports; travel statistics from the Central Statistics Office 
Baseline value:</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2018-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2018-12-31"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator 1</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">By 2018:  Increased percent of provincial capitals connected to the regional highway network to 80% from 70% (in initial year) 
Progress/Status: The outcome will be assessed upon completion of road construction, the work suspension and subsequent termination of the previous contractor hindered the timely achievement of the project outcome. However, the civil work contracts for section 1 and 2 were signed on 16 September 2017 and Notice to proceed (NTP) were issued on 22 Jan 2018. Section 1 (34km) of the Ring Road progress is at 25.22% against the planned progress of 32.5%. Progress of 48km Section 2 is 16.40% against the planned progress of 39.91%. Slow progress of both sections is due to insufficient machinery and staff at the project site. Work is stopped due to cold weather. This project is closed on end November 2018. 
Data Source: MPW and MOTCA traffic counts, surveys and reports; travel statistics from the Central Statistics Office 
Baseline value:</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2018-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2018-12-31"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator 2</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">By 2018:  Reduced travel time between Herat and Mazar-e-Sharif
by 30% for freight traffic 
Progress/Status: The outcome will be assessed upon completion of road construction, the work suspension and subsequent termination of the previous contractor hindered the timely achievement of the project outcome. However, the civil work contracts for section 1 and 2 were signed on 16 September 2017 and Notice to proceed (NTP) were issued on 22 Jan 2018. Section 1 (34km) of the Ring Road progress is at 25.22% against the planned progress of 32.5%. Progress of 48km Section 2 is 16.40% against the planned progress of 39.91%. Slow progress of both sections is due to insufficient machinery and staff at the project site. Work is stopped due to cold weather. Inputs from the grant is completed. 
Data Source: MPW and MOTCA traffic counts, surveys and reports; travel statistics from the Central Statistics Office 
Baseline value:</narrative>
    </description>
