  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project Output/s</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output/s as listed by the project staff.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2  Indicator 1</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: 2. Provision of basic infrastructure needs for about 100 local communities. 
Indicator: By 2016:  233 km of the new road between Qaisar and Laman completed 
Progress/Status: Road project experienced delays. The implementation delayed due to security problem which eventually led to the stoppage of civil works and contract termination by the Contractor. The new contract for sections 1 and 2 signed on 16 September 2017. The grant agreement closing date extended  from December 2016 to 28 November 2018 is approved. the civil work contracts for section 1 and 2 were signed on 16 September 2017 and Notice to proceed (NTP) were issued on 22 Jan 2018. Section 1 (34km) of the Ring Road progress is at 25.22% against the planned progress of 32.5%. Progress of 48km Section 2 is 16.40% against the planned progress of 39.91%. Slow progress of both sections is due to insufficient machinery and staff at the project site. Work is stopped due to cold weather. Works will continue under Grants 0012, and 0081. 
Data Source: Annual MPW Infrastructure Reports 
Actual value:</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="0" year="2010"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2016-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2016-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="233"></target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2  Indicator 2</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: 2. Provision of basic infrastructure needs for about 100 local communities. 
Indicator: By 2016:  New and rehabilitated rural infrastructure for at least 80% of road site communities (baseline data to be collected in initial assessment) 
Progress/Status: Previously, 72 community development subprojects that will benefit 80 communities were approved but were also affected by work stoppage. The EA has to ensure that community development projects will also resume later when the project is back on track.  Works will continue under Grants 0012, and 0081.

 
Data Source: Verification reports conducted by NGO; MOI reports</narrative>
    </description>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2  Indicator 1</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: 2. Provision of basic infrastructure needs for about 100 local communities. 
Indicator: By 2016:  Women&amp;apos;s infrastructure needs addressed in at least 50% of communities. 
Progress/Status: Women&amp;apos;s infrastrtucture needs are included among the 72 Community outreach and development projects in Sec-1 and 2 to be implemented by NGO &#x201c;Afghan Social Development &amp; Training Organization&#x201d; (ASDTO) but were also affected by work stoppage. The implementation of community development projects will be resumed also when the project is back on track. Works will continue under Grants 0012, and 0081. 
Data Source: Verification reports conducted by NGO; MOI reports</narrative>
    </description>
   </indicator>
